## Explanation
For the **RepairCafé Ticketing System**, I built an interactive, component-based user interface using **Next.js** and **React** styled with **Tailwind CSS**. The application features reusable custom components designed to facilitate smooth workflows, manage internal state, react to native browser API events, and implement proper cleanup logic on component unmounting.

### Key Interactive Components

#### 1. Reusable Dropdown Component (`Dropdown.tsx`)
A custom dropdown input designed from scratch to offer a consistent select experience across forms.
*   **State Management**: Manages state for whether the dropdown is open (`isOpen`) and the currently selected value (`selectedValue`).
*   **Outside Click Detection**: To improve user experience, it listens to the document's `mousedown` event to automatically close the dropdown if the user clicks outside. The event listener is registered dynamically only when the dropdown is open and is cleanly removed on unmount.
*   **Code Reference**: [Dropdown.tsx](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/app/components/Dropdown.tsx)

#### 2. Interactive Camera-Based QR Scanner (`QRScanner.tsx`)
This component allows students and admins to quickly scan ticket QR codes to check/update status.
*   **API Interaction & Permissions**: Interacts with the browser's `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` API to request camera access. It handles states such as `checking`, `granted`, or `denied` with appropriate user-facing prompts.
*   **Resource Management & Cleanup**: Crucially, it tracks mounting lifecycle and stops camera media tracks immediately when the scanner is closed or unmounted to prevent memory leaks and keep camera access indicators active.
*   **Code Reference**: [QRScanner.tsx](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/app/components/QRScanner.tsx)

#### 3. Composite Modals (e.g., `GebruikerEditModal.tsx`)
Form components composed of multiple custom sub-components (`EditModal`, `Input`, `Dropdown`) to handle state mutations.
*   **Form Validation**: Maintains state for multiple fields (name, type, username, password) and performs client-side field validation before submitting data to Next.js Server Actions.
*   **Code Reference**: [GebruikerEditModal.tsx](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/app/components/modals/GebruikerEditModal.tsx)

